A thread that becomes ready on a core that idles does not wake it:
the core sleeps on with a thread waiting for its turn there, until something else wakes it.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a thread waits for a turn on a core that idles
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-actor-waits-release

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -238,7 +238,7 @@ void core_notify(struct core *c)
      * whose timer may be set past the change, or whose run queue or turn changed, which takes the core at once
      * if the turn is on spare time or its request is due before the turn's.
      */
-    if (c != core_self() && (c->turn == NULL || __atomic_load_n(&c->in_user, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE))) {
+    if (c != core_self() && (__atomic_load_n(&c->in_user, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE))) {
         c->interrupt_owed = true;
     }
 #else
